Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: disable transaction elimination on Mali-G78

Transaction elimination produces stale tiles on Mali-G78 MP20 (gs101).
Text is the worst affected, being what changes most often between frames,
and the GPU wedges within seconds under a compositor. PAN_MESA_DEBUG=nocrc
avoids both, so gate it on a model quirk instead.

The CRC layout constants are correct for arch 9 and G68 shares them, so the
underlying cause is not the layout. It is not understood yet.

--- a/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.h
@@ -85,6 +85,7 @@
        */
       bool no_hierarchical_tiling;
       bool max_4x_msaa;
+      bool no_crc;
    } quirks;
 };
 
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -828,6 +828,9 @@
    unsigned bytes_per_pixel = MAX2(pres->base.nr_samples, 1) *
                               util_format_get_blocksize(pres->base.format);
 
+   if (dev->model->quirks.no_crc)
+      return false;
+
    return pres->base.bind & PIPE_BIND_RENDER_TARGET && panfrost_is_2d(pres) &&
           bytes_per_pixel <= bytes_per_pixel_max &&
           pres->base.last_level == 0 && !(dev->debug & PAN_DBG_NO_CRC);
